{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "04c1a6dc-3042-48a8-81d2-0a5a162016dc"/*VideoClip*/,
  "Description": "Plays a video file as a clip on the timeline, decoded with FFmpeg.\n\nThe clip's position on the timeline defines when the video plays; trimming and slipping the clip remaps its source range like in a video editor. A [VideoClipPlayer] composites all video clips of a composition — wired into its input or auto-collected — using each clip's Color and BlendMode, with lower layers drawn on top.\n\nOptimize For selects the decode strategy: Fast Seeking (the default) decodes in software with a RAM frame cache for instant scrubbing; Playback Performance decodes zero-copy on the GPU for the smoothest playback of large or 4K footage.\n\nAlso see [PlayVideo] for timeline-independent playback.\n\nThe video's audio track plays too, at Volume. AudioReference exposes it to the audio graph: wire it into an [AudioBus], directly or through a [CombineAudio], to apply group volume, effect inserts and ducking — or leave it unwired and the sound simply plays. Sound follows the picture, so an operator nothing draws stays silent, and Volume 0 skips decoding the audio altogether.\n\nAKA: video, movie, footage, clip, mp4, mkv",
  "SymbolTags": "1",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "27f02af3-06f3-4cb2-8731-2e8777634275"/*BlendMode*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 285.0
      },
      "Description": "Blend mode used when a [VideoClipPlayer] composites this clip over the layers below."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "28f27625-37fe-409a-b6c1-d4eabf6c1eb8"/*Volume*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 90.0
      },
      "Description": "Volume of the video's own sound track.\n\nAt 0 the audio track isn't decoded at all, so a video used purely as a texture costs nothing.",
      "AddPadding": "True",
      "Min": 0.0,
      "ClampMin": true
    },
    {
      "InputId": "31721e18-556b-452b-a8aa-18dbd44af74d"/*Path*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 45.0
      },
      "Description": "Path to the video file.",
      "AddPadding": "True",
      "Usage": "FilePath",
      "FileFilter": "mp4, mov, webm, mpg, mpeg, m4v, mkv, avi, wmv, flv, ts, m2ts, mts, mxf, ogv"
    },
    {
      "InputId": "5eb10090-ae6a-4ae7-9fbd-5bd9ffd13b1b"/*ResyncThreshold*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 135.0
      },
      "Description": "No longer used — timing is frame-exact now. Kept for compatibility with older projects."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "7fb1d490-6c9b-4380-b88c-800d44c16475"/*Color*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 210.0
      },
      "Description": "Tint and opacity used when a [VideoClipPlayer] composites this clip (alpha = opacity).",
      "Min": 0.0,
      "Max": 1.0,
      "ClampMin": true
    },
    {
      "InputId": "f7e8f5f1-3333-409f-92da-573b1f32c0d6"/*OptimizeFor*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 360.0
      },
      "Description": "Selects the decode strategy:\n\nFast Seeking (default): decodes on the CPU and caches recent frames in RAM. Scrubbing back, looping and reverse playback are instant, and the GPU stays free for rendering. Higher CPU load on large frames.\n\nPlayback Performance: decodes on the GPU (D3D11VA) and keeps the frames there — the decoded surface is converted straight to the output texture by a compute shader, with no GPU→CPU read-back (zero-copy). Smoothest playback for large / 4K long-GOP footage, but random seeks re-decode from the previous keyframe. Automatically falls back to software decode when the codec has no GPU decoder (e.g. ProRes, HAP) or the driver rejects it."
    }
  ],
  "SymbolChildUis": [],
  "OutputUis": [
    {
      "OutputId": "eb954aeb-535b-4b22-ac49-858f71bdaac4"/*Texture*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 300.0,
        "Y": 200.0
      }
    },
    {
      "OutputId": "d9da88fb-a5ac-451f-8727-a8ce126432d8"/*AudioReference*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 300.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      }
    }
  ]
}